  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origin and Original Terms
    
    Stillness-Bound was created during the Clever Ice Age as a merchant charter granting the Aureate, the guild-faction rooted in The Still Pools, exclusive rights to move goods through those waters without taxation or interference. Authority under the charter was authenticated by guild seal and the aurora-touched signature of Bursar Ingnao shi'Beacon. In its original form, Stillness-Bound was straightforward commercial protection — a libertarian instrument, narrow in scope.
    
    It did not remain narrow.
    
    ## Amendments by Crisis
    
    The Orca Incursion prompted the first substantive amendment, which enshrined the Thaw-Paths Medallion — a palm-sized aurora-glass artifact carved with glowing pathways — as a marker of safe passage through threatened trade routes. The Medallion was lost or proved ineffective; traders died regardless, their bodies recovered from tidal pools bearing orca-marks. The charter offered no remedy.
    
    The Aurora-touched succession crisis that followed — the fracture between Prism-Ascending and Depth-Keeper after Meridian-of-the-First-Light's death — was not prevented by Stillness-Bound's terms, but was *commemorated* by them. A second amendment inscribed the crisis into the charter's language without altering its operative clauses.
    
    During the Darkening, a seventeen-day aurora failure, Aureate merchants invoked Stillness-Bound to claim priority over supply reserves. The charter did not support this reading. It was amended again — not to clarify the question but to commemorate the event that raised it. This pattern — crisis, failed application, commemorative amendment — repeated for at least three crown-contested moments and one disaster the charter references only obliquely.
    
    Stillness-Bound now subsumes the earlier Dawn-Marked legal code and commemorates, in addition to the above, the trade festival known as Accord (light-blessed) and the succession dispute designated Of The High Tier. Its original commercial terms are buried beneath layers of addendum and witness-mark. The thirty-first addendum is entirely illegible beneath commemorative inscriptions for the Thaw-Paths dead.
    
    ## Enforcement
    
    The Council of Luminaries enforces Stillness-Bound when the aurora is clear enough to read by. When overcast, enforcement lapses and goods move without restriction. Whether this conditional enforcement is a flaw or a feature designed by the Aureate remains disputed.
    
    ## Modern Adoptions
    
    The Accord of Still Pools and Frost Zenith, a treaty between the Aureate and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, adopted Stillness-Bound as its legal framework while acknowledging in its preamble that Ingnao shi'Beacon's original charter was insufficient for current conditions. Under the accord's terms, fire-core warranty provisions requiring three-day replacement of defective cores were restored from lapse, with the Courier Corps designated to adjudicate violations. In practice, post-Calving demand has rendered the three-day mandate unenforceable; adjudication forms are substituted for actual replacements.
    
    A separate accord between Holdborn, an Aurora-chartered ice-threshold faction, and the Nightshelf guild Weal' Clique~ over joint stewardship of The Beacon Stack also adopted Stillness-Bound as its adjudication framework, referencing the seventeenth and twenty-third addenda.
    
    ## The Medallion Provisions
    
    The Communion, an elt-sworn Nightshelf faction, invoked Stillness-Bound to place the Thaw-Paths Medallion under non-contact protection at ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis~ after the artifact's last restorer died. The Aurora Stack separately invoked the same provision to protect the Medallion at The Dawn Terrace after it began glowing without aurora-light on the anniversary of a Wake-Singer breach at The Fissured Smelt~.
    
    An Exchange auditor subsequently breached the non-contact provision, removing the Medallion from the Lens-Cathedral during an investigation into a Midnight Claws confession and carrying it out of the Stack entirely. No adjudication under Stillness-Bound precedent has followed. Whether any is forthcoming depends, presumably, on the sky.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771581865023_0", anchor: "a seventeen-day aurora failure", text: "Seventeen again. I stated the number here as though settled, but my own Darkening annotation argues the boundary between seventeen and eighteen depends on what the ice could witness versus what it could not. The charter's commemorative inscription presumably records the Aureate's count, not the ice's. Whether the Aureate had reason to prefer a shorter duration is a question I leave in the margin rather than the text.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771581865023_1", anchor: "crisis, failed application, commemorative amendment", text: "The same mechanism I documented in Foedus∴vincu at civilizational scale: damage becoming structure, wounds becoming load-bearing. But Foedus∴vincu at least produced a functional legal framework from its scars. Stillness-Bound produced a document that cannot be read. The Nightshelf carved their dead into binding law. The Aureate carved their dead into binding law and then kept adding dead until the law disappeared. The impulse is identical. The discipline is not.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771581865023_2", anchor: "carrying it out of the Stack entirely", text: "An unnamed courier vanished carrying it between civilizations. Yunjoushong vanished carrying it toward Midway Shelf. Now an Exchange auditor has carried it out of the Stack, and no adjudication has followed — which could mean institutional paralysis, or could mean there is no one left to adjudicate because the auditor has joined the pattern. I have asked, through channels. The silence is its own answer.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771581865023_3", anchor: "enforcement lapses and goods move without restriction", text: "During the Long Dark, enforcement lapses for months. The Aureate's original Still Pools monopoly was forged in the Clever Ice Age, when Long Darks were longer. One wonders what moved through those waters, untaxed and unwitnessed, while the aurora was elsewhere.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
